# Build output. Only bin/ — the rest of build/ is the platform asset source
# (app icon, Info.plist templates, NSIS installer scripts) and has to be
# committed: Wails silently regenerates whatever is missing from its own
# defaults, so an uncommitted appicon.png means CI ships the Wails logo.
/build/bin/
# dist itself is build output, but the directory has to exist in a fresh clone:
# main.go does `//go:embed all:frontend/dist`, and an absent directory makes
# `go vet`, `go build` and `go test ./...` all fail before doing any work. The
# `all:` prefix matches dotfiles, so an empty .gitkeep is enough to satisfy it.
/frontend/dist/*
!/frontend/dist/.gitkeep
/frontend/node_modules/

# Wails generates these from the Go bindings on every build; they are derived,
# not authored.
/frontend/wailsjs/

# Go
*.test
# Coverage profiles. Narrow rather than a bare *.out, which also swallowed every
# captured stdout in testdata/windows/golden — the golden files would have been
# committed as .err/.exit metadata with the actual data silently missing.
*.cover.out
coverage.out
profile.out

# Developer credentials for the manual integration hosts. In .gitignore rather
# than .git/info/exclude on purpose: this one should be visible to anyone who
# clones, because the failure mode of not knowing about it is committing a
# password. testdata/windows/env_guard_test.go fails if it is ever tracked.
.env.local
*.env.local
/testdata/windows/id_*

# Python (build/make-icons.py)
__pycache__/

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# 디버깅용으로 주고받는 스크린샷. 저장소에 들어갈 것이 아니다.
*.png
!build/**/*.png
!frontend/**/*.png
